! mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap -- printed page 99:
! "***** CHANNEL-UNIT STATUS TABLE DEFINITION *****".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.106, header read not assumed: the
! top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11C11IPL  CARD ID
! AA000001  DIST. OF 3701  3701  PAGE NUMBER 99".
!
! FIFTY-TWO LINES, AND THE COUNT WAS CONFIRMED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! rightmost column prints the card serial: lines 1-7 are AA000001 to
! AA000007 and lines 8-52 are BA000001 to BA000045, so for the BA
! series the line number is the serial plus seven.  BA000045 is the
! last printed row and it is line 52.
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS.  Thirty-four of the fifty-two
! lines (19-52) are SYN cards and NOT ONE of them compiles a word.
! Two lines compile storage -- 9 and 10 -- and they are punch card
! images, not program (see SUBSTITUTIONS below).  So this deck's
! entire check surface is THIRTY-FOUR SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING ROWS,
! which is printed p.24's convention and the one p.98 used: a SYN
! prints its VALUE in the LOCATION column and no word, so it is
! checked in !SYM and must not be faked into a !CHECK.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  It is the start of a SECOND punched deck inside
! the SAME assembly.  Printed p.98 line 36 is "X IN END SYN,$" at
! 005466.00; line 9 HERE compiles at that very location, so the
! location counter never restarted, and this page's own header reads
! "PUNID 11C11IPL" -- the previous deck's identification -- which
! line 13 then changes to 11D11MCP.  That is exactly the pattern
! printed pp.13/15/37 recorded for the IPL-to-MCP handoff.  Lines
! 7-14 are punch control (PRNS, PUNFUL, two card images, SLC,
! PUNORG, PUNID, RESEQ); lines 15-18 are the boxed heading; lines
! 19-52 are the table.
!
! FIRST PRINTED LOCATION on the page is 005466.00 (line 9, not
! transcribed).  FIRST AND LAST TRANSCRIBED LOCATIONS are the SLC's
! 215000.00 (line 11) and the symbol values, which all lie in word
! zero: 000000.00+ (line 19) through 000000.77+ (line 51), with line
! 52 at 000000.40+.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) LINES 7-10 ARE TRANSCRIBED SINCE 2026-11-10: PRNS, PUNFUL and the
!     two "(CC*)DD(BU,,12)" header cards, "B        HED, REP, 11D11MCP,
!     LOAD,," and the 11D11MCP card, at 005466.00 and 005476.34.  They
!     were left out while strap_asm refused entry mode CC.
!     Their blanks are MEASURED in the ink (PDF 106 at 300 dpi, the
!     print's fixed pitch of 30 px per cell): "B" in cell 16, "HED" from
!     cell 25, the "*" in cell 61; the second's name from cell 43 and its
!     "*" in 51.  So 8 blanks after the B, 27 before the name: MCP's
!     control-card form (C22-6678-1 pp.7-10), the name in columns
!     73-80.  The 45 characters of the first are also fixed by the
!     printed locations.  tests/check_strap2_punch.py A4-A7.
!     Under PUNFUL they are punched as one full card and NOT loaded
!     (C28-6129 pp.23, 36).  ONE STAND-IN: "SLC, (8)5466.0" before them,
!     X IN END, the counter p.98 leaves (p.98 ends with UNTAIL, not END:
!     one assembly).  Line 11's SLC then comes under PUNFUL, the chart OS
!     "1ST SLC" (C22-6729 p.152): it stores the counter and punches no
!     zeros -- which is what fixes "1ST" as first since PUNFUL (see
!     strap/strap2/punch.py slc).
!
! (2) LINES 1-6 AND 15-18 COMPILE NOTHING AND ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED:
!     1-6 are the title block (IBM 7030 MASTER CONTROL PROGRAM /
!     INTERNATIONAL BUSINESS MACHINES CORP. / DEPT. 271, BLDG. 705 /
!     POUGHKEEPSIE,N.Y. / MARCH 15, 1963), and 15-18 are the asterisk
!     box around the heading.
!
! (3) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  The NAME column prints "S UN A A", "S CH AVL", "S CH OP",
!     "S MULTI", "S DISP O", "S UN AVL", "S UN ASG", "S UN SUP",
!     "S SET UP", "S OWNER", "S SETDN", "S SEL", "S VER", "S SEOP",
!     "S CNS SG", "S U DENS", "S C MODE", "S EQUIP", "S UNIT",
!     "S UNIT K", "S ELG", "S MOUNT", "S REW", "S I MNT", "S RD",
!     "S WR", "S SPACE", "S CTL", "S REL", "S OVRES", "S ARC AD";
!     only "STATI" and "SUNRES" are printed closed up.  Line 20's
!     STATEMENT column likewise prints "SYN, S UN A A".
!
! (4) A SYN VALUE WRITTEN ".26" IS WRITTEN 0.26, p.98's convention
!     (3).  Lines 23, 25, 36, 44, 48, 49 and 50 print the word
!     number as empty where it is zero.
!
! (5) NOTHING ELSE.  Among the lines this deck DOES transcribe --
!     11-14 and 19-52 -- no printed spelling was refused by
!     strap_asm.  Lines 9 and 10 were, and that is omission (1).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE GLYPHS, AND HOW EACH DISPUTED ONE WAS SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY LOCATION ON THIS PAGE IS AN OCTAL FIELD and prints as
! "000000.NN+".  A round glyph there is a 0 with certainty, and the
! page prints a great many of them open on the right: line 19's
! location renders to the eye at 1200 dpi as "000000.0C+" and line
! 20's as "000000.CC+".  They are all zeros.  That same ink level
! calibrates the NAME column beside it, which is where the C/O/0
! trouble actually lives.
!
! >>> THE NAMES ARE CORROBORATED BY A PRIMARY SOURCE, which is the
! unusual thing about this page.  C22-6728-1, "MCP System Analysis
! Guide", Appendix A "Symbolic I-O Control Tables", printed pp.261-
! 267 (PDF page = printed page), tabulates the channel status table,
! the unit status table and their bit symbols.  THIRTY-THREE OF THE
! THIRTY-FOUR NAMES HERE, AND THEIR BIT POSITIONS, APPEAR THERE:
!
!   .00-.17 SUNAA   .25 SCHAVL  .26 SCHOP   .27 SMULTI  .28 SUNAVL
!   .29 SUNASG  .30 SUNSUP  .31 SSETUP  .32 SOWNER  .46 SSEOP
!   .50-.51 SCMODE  .52-.55 SEQUIP  .57 SRD  .58 SWR  .60 SCTL
!   .61 SREL  .62 SUNRES  .63 SOVRES  .32-.49 SARCAD
!   .56-.58 SUNIT  .59-.62 SUNITK  .26 STATI  .27 SDISPO
!   .33 SSETDN  .39 SSEL  .40 SVER  .47 SCNSSG  .50 SELG
!   .51 SMOUNT  .52 SREW  .53 SIMNT  .59 SSPACE
!
! That settles by document, not by squinting, the four glyph pairs
! this page cannot decide by shape:
!   line 25's last character -- "S DISP O" or "S DISP C"?  Appendix
!     A, printed p.265: ".27 SDISPO, 0 Tape mounted / 1 No tape
!     mounted".  It is an O.
!   line 30 -- the first letter of "OWNER" prints open-right and is
!     indistinguishable from the C of line 35's "S CNS SG".
!     Appendix A printed p.262: ".32 SOWNER".  The row's own comment
!     says "-PRIORITY LEVEL,  OWNERSHIP".
!   line 51 -- "S OVRES" likewise; Appendix A printed p.264 ".63
!     SOVRES", comment "-OVERLAPPED RESERVE INDICATOR".
!   line 34 -- "S SEOP"; Appendix A printed p.266 ".46 SSEOP".
! The C/D pair gave no trouble here: line 31's SETDN, line 36's
! DENS, line 37's MODE, line 45's RD and line 52's AD all print the
! straight vertical left stem and squared corners, plainly unlike
! the round stemless C of SCNSSG and SCMODE in the same rows.
!
! >>> TWO PLACES WHERE THE LISTING AND APPENDIX A DISAGREE.  Both
! are recorded, neither is "corrected" -- the listing is the primary
! artifact and C22-6728-1 is a LATER REVISION of a different
! document.
!   (a) LINE 36 IS "S U DENS", six characters, and Appendix A
!       printed p.266 calls bit .49 SUNDENS, seven.  Rendered at
!       1800 dpi the NAME column shows S, blank, U, blank, D, E, N,
!       S with no N before the D.  Transcribed as printed: SUDENS.
!   (b) LINE 19 IS "SYN(BU,25)", confirmed twice on its own row --
!       the data-description column prints "BU,31 ,10" and 0o31 is
!       25 -- while Appendix A printed p.261 gives SUNAA as bits
!       .00-.17, eighteen.  Transcribed as printed: 25.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT ACTUALLY CHECKS WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * NO ROW IS AN INDEPENDENT BINARY CHECK, because there are no
!   rows.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints "+00000000" on all
!   thirty-four SYN lines and that is the column working correctly
!   on a definitions page, not a crop in the wrong place.
! * EACH SYMBOL IS CHECKED TWICE BY THE PAGE ITSELF, and this is a
!   real check of the digits though not of the card: the STATEMENT
!   column prints the bit offset in DECIMAL and the LOCATION column
!   prints the same offset in OCTAL, and all thirty-four agree
!   (0.25/.31, 0.46/.56, 0.63/.77, and so on).  The data-description
!   column gives a third rendering of the LENGTH for the seven
!   multi-bit fields: BU,31=25, BU,02=2, BU,04=4, BU,03=3, BU,22=18.
! * THREE SYMBOLS ARE CHECKED AGAINST ANOTHER TRANSCRIBED PAGE.
!   Printed p.98 lines 24, 25 and 26 declare STATI SYN(BU,1),.26,
!   SIMNT SYN(BU,1),.53 and S MOUNT SYN(BU,1),.51 in the OTHER deck
!   of this same assembly.  All three agree with this page exactly.
!   That is three of thirty-four.
! * APPENDIX A CORROBORATES THIRTY-THREE SPELLINGS AND BIT
!   POSITIONS but it is a different document and a later revision,
!   with the two disagreements above.  Treat it as corroboration of
!   the SPELLINGS -- which listing_oracle can never check -- and not
!   as verification of the transcription.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE of the fifty-two line numbers carries an asterisk right
! after it ("19*", "52*").  That is not the mark printed pp.3/37/38/
! 39/88/98 carry, which sits after the LOCATION; this one is in the
! line-number column and is on every line of the page.  Lines 8 and
! 10 carry a SECOND asterisk, in the location column, which is the
! familiar one.  No asterisk changes a compiled bit.

        SLC, (8)5466.0              ! STAND-IN: X IN END, the counter p.98 leaves (one assembly, no END); line 9 prints 005466.00
        PRNS                        ! line  7
        PUNFUL                      ! line  8
        (CC*)DD(BU,,12),B        HED, REP, 11D11MCP, LOAD,,          *   ! line  9  005466.00
        (CC*)DD(BU,,12),                           11D11MCP*   ! line 10  005476.34
        SLC, (8)215000.0            ! line 11 -80K

        PUNORG                      ! line 12
        PUNID, 11D11MCP             ! line 13
        RESEQ                       ! line 14

! ---- ***** CHANNEL-UNIT STATUS TABLE DEFINITION ***** (lines 15-17)
SUNAA   SYN(BU,25), 0.0             ! line 19 -UNIT AREA TABLE FIELD
SUNA    SYN, SUNAA                  ! line 20 -UNIT AREA TABLE FIELD
SCHAVL  SYN(BU,1), 0.25             ! line 21 -CHANNEL AVAILABILITY,
                                     !           CHANNEL STATUS
SCHOP   SYN(BU,1), 0.26             ! line 22 -CHAN OPERATING, CHAN
                                     !           STATUS
STATI   SYN(BU,1), 0.26             ! line 23 -TYPE OF TAPE MTED.
                                     !           0 SCRATCH 1 SPECIF
SMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27             ! line 24 -MULTI-UNIT CHAN, CHAN
                                     !           STATUS
SDISPO  SYN(BU,1), 0.27             ! line 25 -UST REEL TUPE  (sic,
                                     !           printed exactly so)
SUNAVL  SYN(BU,1), 0.28             ! line 26 -UNIT AVAILABILITY,
                                     !           UNIT STATUS
SUNASG  SYN(BU,1), 0.29             ! line 27 -UNIT ASSIGNMENT,
                                     !           UNIT STATUS
SUNSUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.30             ! line 28 -UNIT SUPPRESSION,
                                     !           UNIT STATUS
SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31             ! line 29 -PSEUDO-OP SET-UP,
                                     !           UNIT STATUS
SOWNER  SYN(BU,1), 0.32             ! line 30 -PRIORITY LEVEL,
                                     !           OWNERSHIP
SSETDN  SYN(BU,1), 0.33             ! line 31 -ORIGINAL DENSITY SET
                                     !           INDICATOR
SSEL    SYN(BU,1), 0.39             ! line 32 -SELECT FILE STATUS
SVER    SYN(BU,1), 0.40             ! line 33 -VERIFY FILE STATUS
SSEOP   SYN(BU,1), 0.46             ! line 34 -SUPP END OF OP STATUS
SCNSSG  SYN(BU,1), 0.47             ! line 35 -CONSOLE SIGNAL, FILE
                                     !           STATUS
SUDENS  SYN(BU,1), 0.49             ! line 36 -CURRENT DENSITY OF UNIT
SCMODE  SYN(BU,2), 0.50             ! line 37 -CHANNEL MODE
SEQUIP  SYN(BU,4), 0.52             ! line 38 -EQUIPMENT
SUNIT   SYN(BU,3), 0.56             ! line 39 -UNIT (MULTI UNIT
                                     !           CHANNEL ONLY)
SUNITK  SYN(BU,4), 0.59             ! line 40 -UNIT COUNT(MULTI UNIT
                                     !           CHANNEL ONLY)
SELG    SYN(BU,1), 0.50             ! line 41 -ERASE LONG GAP
SMOUNT  SYN(BU,1), 0.51             ! line 42 -MOUNT TAPE
SREW    SYN(BU,1), 0.52             ! line 43 -REWIND TAPE
SIMNT   SYN(BU,1), 0.53             ! line 44 -INITIAL MOUNTING OF REEL
SRD     SYN(BU,1), 0.57             ! line 45 -READ, OPERATION STATUS
SWR     SYN(BU,1), 0.58             ! line 46 -WRITE, OPERATION STATUS
SSPACE  SYN(BU,1), 0.59             ! line 47 -SPACE FILE STATUS
SCTL    SYN(BU,1), 0.60             ! line 48 -CONTROL - OPERATION
                                     !           STATUS
SREL    SYN(BU,1), 0.61             ! line 49 -RELEASE - OPERATION
                                     !           STATUS
SUNRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.62             ! line 50 -NOT OVERLAP RESERVED BIT
SOVRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.63             ! line 51 -OVERLAPPED RESERVE
                                     !           INDICATOR
SARCAD  SYN(BU,18), 0.32            ! line 52 -ARC ADDRESS (DISK)

