!
! THE OTHER PRINTED LINES, for the record:
!   line  9  005466.00   (CC*)DD(BU,,12),B      HED, REP, 11D11MCP, LOAD,
!   line 10  005476.34 * (CC*)DD(BU,,12),       11D11<truncated by
!                                                  the crop>
!   line 11  215000.00   SLC,(8)215000.        - 80K
!
! FIELDS THAT OVERLAY.  Several bits carry two names because the
! single-unit CHANNEL status entry and the multi-unit UNIT status
! entry are two readings of the same word: .26 is SCHOP and STATI,
! .27 is SMULTI and SDISPO, .32 is SOWNER and the start of SARCAD,
! .50 is SELG and the start of SCMODE, .52 is SREW and the start of
! SEQUIP, .59 is SSPACE and the start of SUNITK.  Appendix A's
! separate "Channel Status Table Entry" and "Unit Status Table
! Entry" headings say the same thing.  It is not a mis-read.

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 99 -----------------
! Thirty-four symbols and no rows: a SYN deposits no storage word,
! so there is nothing for a !CHECK to look at.  The trailing "+"
! the page prints after every location is the SIGN, printed as a
! suffix the way printed p.84's negative SYN prints "000001.00-".
! It is dropped here because listing_oracle.loc_bits parses a
! location as "word.bit" and has no sign field, and because every
! landed deck records the bare NNNNNN.NN.
!SYM   SUNAA    000000.00
!SYM   SUNA     000000.00
!SYM   SCHAVL   000000.31
!SYM   SCHOP    000000.32
!SYM   STATI    000000.32
!SYM   SMULTI   000000.33
!SYM   SDISPO   000000.33
